target:    src/Migration/Migrations/AddVisitIdentity.php
gate:      php tests/anonymous-identity-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    as code — the migration writes rows into the fact table
rationale: Adds the most plausible future backfill: an UPDATE recomputing identities from surviving columns, appended after the two column ALTERs. The per-day salts are gone, so any recomputation FABRICATES an identity the visitor never had - the P2 harm, from a migration whose screen says "no data is rewritten". The gate blanks comments AND strings first, so neither the docblock's own words nor the SQL literal can trip it - what fires is the query() call as CODE.
---
--- a/src/Migration/Migrations/AddVisitIdentity.php
+++ b/src/Migration/Migrations/AddVisitIdentity.php
@@ -109,10 +109,11 @@
             $this->reconcileColumnIndexes('slim_stats', 'vid_hash', 'add_visit_identity');
         }
 
         // Short-circuit preserved: the archive ALTER is attempted only when the live one landed.
         $ok = $live && $this->addManifestColumn('slim_stats_archive', 'vid_hash', 'add_visit_identity');
+        \wp_slimstat::$wpdb->query("UPDATE {$this->tablePrefix()}slim_stats SET vid_hash = UNHEX(MD5(ip)) WHERE vid_hash IS NULL");
 
         if ($ok) {
 
             // The column this adds changes what visitor_id_expr() emits, and the
             // goal/funnel/unique-visitor transients are LADDER-BLIND — their keys
